          "guid": "mt14ll36qz6euyv8",
          "message": {
            "text": "Extracted, not rewritten — the positioning primitives moved verbatim so behavior is provably unchanged.\n\noverlay.ts was 1143 LOC across three concern-clusters; positionAnchored/autoReposition are the cleanest to split because they're standalone public exports (any element, no overlay lifecycle). The code moved byte-for-byte (including the KF-507 \"fix position:fixed before measuring\" ordering); overlay.ts imports autoReposition for popover/tooltip and re-exports all four symbols, so the kerfjs/overlay public surface and the bundle are unchanged. Verified: overlay bundle stayed 16.11 KB, and the overlay browser spec (popover left-align + tooltip, which exercise this code) passes on chromium.\n",
            "markdown": "Extracted, not rewritten — the positioning primitives moved verbatim so behavior is provably unchanged.\n\noverlay.ts was 1143 LOC across three concern-clusters; `positionAnchored`/`autoReposition` are the cleanest to split because they're standalone public exports (any element, no overlay lifecycle). The code moved byte-for-byte (including the KF-507 \"fix position:fixed before measuring\" ordering); overlay.ts imports `autoReposition` for popover/tooltip and re-exports all four symbols, so the `kerfjs/overlay` public surface and the bundle are unchanged. Verified: overlay bundle stayed 16.11 KB, and the overlay browser spec (popover left-align + tooltip, which exercise this code) passes on chromium.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/overlay-position.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1,
                  "endLine": 9,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "/**\n * Anchored positioning primitives for `kerfjs/overlay` — position an element\n * relative to an anchor, with viewport flip + clamp. These are standalone: they\n * take any element and have no overlay lifecycle, so `popover()` / `tooltip()`\n * build on them but you can also position your own element (an inline hint, a\n * custom menu). Re-exported from `src/overlay.ts` so the public `kerfjs/overlay`\n * surface is unchanged (KF-511 split out of overlay.ts's dialog + toast code).\n */\n"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
